PRE-EXISTING, OUT-OF-SCOPE BUILD/TEST BLOCKERS  (disclosed, NOT masked, NOT mine)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Honesty rule #1 (No red-as-green): the green BUILD/TEST above were obtained after
temporarily neutralizing THREE pre-existing, unmodified, out-of-scope defects that
are unrelated to this page and that I did NOT author and did NOT commit. On the
committed tree (these files restored to their original state) the FULL `xcodebuild
build` / `test` are RED=65 SOLELY because of them. They are Swift-6.3/Xcode-26.5
toolchain-compat regressions in OTHER features:

  1. Sources/Features/Driving/DriveScorePage.Panels.swift:25  (app target — blocks `build`)
       error: cannot convert 'LocalizedStringKey' to 'String.LocalizationValue'
       cause: `String(localized: model.overallTrend.labelKey)` — `String(localized:)` does not
              accept a LocalizedStringKey under this toolchain. (My own code deliberately avoids
              this exact pattern: PeriodCompareMetric exposes `titleKeyName: String` for
              String.LocalizationValue use — see PeriodComparePage.Charts.swift `summary`.)
  2. Tests/Unit/Features/Admin/VehicleCostPageModelTests.swift:10,21,156 (test bundle — blocks `test`)
       main-actor-isolated default in a nonisolated nested struct; + XCTAssertEqual(accuracy:) on Date.
  3. Tests/Unit/Features/Admin/GDPRExportPageModelTests.swift:20      (test bundle — blocks `test`)
       call to a main-actor-isolated static method in a synchronous nonisolated context.

Verification method: each blocker was temporarily reduced to a compiling stub ONLY to run the
real build + the real test suite, then fully reverted (`git checkout`). `git status` confirms the
committed change set contains ONLY the in-scope files listed above — none of the three blockers.
This mirrors the accepted sibling methodology (see apple-page-analytics-FleetComparePage.log,
which documents an analogous pre-existing out-of-scope RED and still ends STATUS=DONE).

